# SABOTAGE: UXD-05 attempt-3 (T11-verdict.json's `strongest_attack` against attempt 2's
# `39ebc4d`; ADR-047 §10a row 19) — head substitution in `resolves_to_kernel?/3` re-resolves
# the substituted alias WITHOUT the reference's remaining segments, so a renamed PARENT
# namespace no longer rebuilds the kernel path: `alias Samen.AI, as: A` followed by
# `A.Agent.start(...)`, `apply(A.Agent, :start, [...])`, or a further `alias A.Agent, as: B`
# evades the F-4 raw-spawn lock again — the exact class that survived attempts 1 and 2.
# Renames of the kernel MODULE itself, and chains of them, are UNAFFECTED: this patch
# reopens only the PREFIX-rename case.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/agent_coverage_verifier_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: RED FIXTURE (UXD-05, attempt 3) — a PARENT-namespace rename evades the DIRECT-CALL form
